<!-- ================= 4. BRUNCH & BREAKFAST ================= -->
<section id="brunch" class="cltp-sec cltp-sec--band" style="--sec:#56B85A;">
  <div class="cltp-wrap">
    <p class="cltp-kicker">Mornings Done Right</p>
    <h2>Where Charlotte Eats in the Morning</h2>
    <div class="cltp-prose">
      <p>Charlotte brunch is a competitive sport — the waits at the big names prove it. These are the morning places we actually send people to, from counter-service bakeries to chef-driven Southern spreads. Which of them serve <a href="/brunch-charlotte-nc/">brunch in Charlotte</a> on which days &mdash; and whether you can walk in, join a waitlist or need to book &mdash; is a separate guide.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cltp-rows">
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>Haberdish <span class="cltp-when">$$ · NoDa</span></h3><p>Weekend brunch done the Haberdish way: fried chicken and waffles, smoked trout deviled eggs, and a cinnamon roll built for the table.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="uptown-yolk">Uptown Yolk <span class="cltp-when">$$ · South End</span></h3><p>Southern breakfast — Mojo Hash, shrimp and grits — from chef Greg Collier, a 2023 James Beard finalist for Outstanding Chef and the most decorated name in Charlotte food.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="snooze-an-am-eatery">Snooze, an A.M. Eatery <span class="cltp-when">$$ · Plaza Midwood +</span></h3><p>Pancake flights and Benedict duos daily until mid-afternoon — expect a weekend wait at all three Charlotte locations.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="the-original-pancake-house">The Original Pancake House <span class="cltp-when">$ · Midtown</span></h3><p>The classic: scratch batters made daily, the famous oven-baked Apple Pancake, and doors open at 7am.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="amelies-french-bakery">Amélie&#8217;s French Bakery <span class="cltp-when">$ · NoDa +</span></h3><p>The iconic Charlotte bakery — salted caramel brownies, croissants, quiche — in its flea-market-Paris flagship on 36th Street.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="easy-like-sunday">Easy Like Sunday <span class="cltp-when">$$ · South End +</span></h3><p>All-day brunch, every day — ricotta-stuffed French toast, ube pancakes, and a proper brunch burger.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="sunflour-baking-company">Sunflour Baking Company <span class="cltp-when">$ · Elizabeth +</span></h3><p>Neighborhood scratch bakery — breakfast sandwiches on house-baked bread and cinnamon rolls without the scene.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cltp-prose">
      <p>Going fancier? <strong>Supperland</strong> does a lavish reservation-only Sunday brunch with tableside cinnamon rolls, and <strong>La Belle Hélène</strong> pours Bananas Foster French toast in full Parisian splendor on weekends.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= 5. DATE NIGHT ================= -->
<section id="date-night" class="cltp-sec" style="--sec:#4C3957;">
  <div class="cltp-wrap">
    <p class="cltp-kicker">Table for Two</p>
    <h2>Romantic Restaurants in Charlotte: Date Night &amp; Special Occasions</h2>
    <div class="cltp-prose">
      <p>Anniversary, proposal, or just a night that needs to land — these are the romantic restaurants in Charlotte we&#8217;d book, from candlelit bungalow to Michelin-starred counter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cltp-rows">
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>The Fig Tree <span class="cltp-when">$$$$ · Elizabeth</span></h3><p>The reigning champion of Charlotte proposals — fireplace dining rooms in a century-old Craftsman house and a wine list to match the moment.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>Counter‑ <span class="cltp-when">$$$$ · Wesley Heights</span></h3><p>Book the Michelin-starred, music-paired tasting menu when the occasion is big enough to deserve a story afterward.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>Supperland <span class="cltp-when">$$$ · Plaza Midwood</span></h3><p>Steak dinner in a candlelit former chapel with award-winning cocktails — the most romantic room in the city, full stop.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="beef-n-bottle">Beef &#8216;N Bottle <span class="cltp-when">$$$ · South Blvd</span></h3><p>Red leather booths, low light, and filets that haven&#8217;t missed since 1958 — retro romance, no irony required.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>Fin &amp; Fino <span class="cltp-when">$$$ · Uptown</span></h3><p>Oysters, a champagne cart, and theater tickets a block away — the polished Uptown date, solved.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3>Hestia Rooftop <span class="cltp-when">$$$ · Ballantyne</span></h3><p>Sixteen floors up with sunset views to the skyline — south Charlotte&#8217;s view-with-dinner move.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= 6. FOOD EVENTS ================= -->
<section id="events" class="cltp-sec cltp-sec--band" style="--sec:#E29C04;">
  <div class="cltp-wrap">
    <p class="cltp-kicker">Mark the Calendar</p>
    <h2>Charlotte Food Events &amp; Restaurant Week</h2>
    <div class="cltp-prose">
      <p>Charlotte&#8217;s food calendar has a rhythm to it — these are the recurring events worth planning a meal (or a weekend) around:</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cltp-rows">
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3><a href="/explore-charlotte-restaurant-week-july-2026-dining-guide/">Queen&#8217;s Feast: Charlotte Restaurant Week</a> <span class="cltp-when">Jan &amp; July</span></h3><p>Ten days, twice a year, 120+ restaurants doing three-course prix fixe menus — read our guide to picking your reservations wisely.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3><a href="/greek-festival-charlotte/">Yiasou Greek Festival</a> <span class="cltp-when">September</span></h3><p>One of the Southeast&#8217;s biggest Greek festivals — gyros, loukoumades, and dancing at Holy Trinity Greek Orthodox Cathedral every September.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="taste-of-charlotte">Taste of Charlotte <span class="cltp-when">June</span></h3><p>Three days of restaurant tastings along Tryon Street Uptown every summer.</p></div></div>
      <div class="cltp-row"><span class="cltp-row-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="cltp-row-body"><h3 id="charlotte-wine-food-week">Charlotte Wine + Food Week <span class="cltp-when">April</span></h3><p>A week of tastings and chef dinners that has quietly raised hundreds of thousands for children&#8217;s charities across nearly four decades.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= 7. FAQ ================= -->
<section id="faq" class="cltp-sec cltp-faq" style="--sec:#343A40;">
  <div class="cltp-wrap">
    <p class="cltp-kicker">Quick Answers</p>
    <h2>Charlotte Restaurants: FAQ</h2>
    <div class="cltp-prose" style="margin-top:18px;">
      <details>
        <summary>What food is Charlotte, NC known for?</summary>
        <p>Southern cooking is the backbone — fried chicken, shrimp and grits, and Carolina barbecue (Midwood Smokehouse is the standard-bearer), plus regional oddities like livermush. But modern Charlotte is just as much about its international kitchens along Central Avenue and South Boulevard, a craft-brewery scene in the dozens, and a fine-dining class that earned the city its first Michelin star in 2025.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What are the best restaurants in Charlotte right now?</summary>
        <p>Our current short list: Counter‑ (the city&#8217;s first Michelin star), Haberdish, Supperland, Lang Van (Michelin Bib Gourmand), The Fig Tree, and Rada in Myers Park. The full ranked rundown is in <a href="#essentials">The Essentials</a> section of this guide, and we update it as the scene changes.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where should I eat in Uptown Charlotte?</summary>
        <p>Church and Union and La Belle Hélène for a big night, Fin &amp; Fino for seafood before a show, Sea Level NC for oysters and happy hour, and Mert&#8217;s Heart &amp; Soul for soul food before a Hornets game. See the <a href="#uptown">Uptown section</a> for the full list.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What restaurants are open late in Charlotte?</summary>
        <p>Midnight Diner (near Spectrum Center) and RedEye Diner (Queen City Quarter) are both open 24/7 Uptown. Fuel Pizza in Plaza Midwood slings slices until 2–3am on weekends, and Cook Out drive-thrus across the city run until 3–4am.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What new restaurants have opened in Charlotte?</summary>
        <p>The 2026 class is strong: flora in South End, Uchi + Uchibā and Maman in Plaza Midwood, Grey&#8217;s Diner on The Plaza, Italo Uptown, and DaBaby&#8217;s No Knife Chicken &amp; Waffles, which opened on Atando Ave in north Charlotte on September 7. We keep the <a href="#new">New &amp; Noteworthy</a> section updated as openings happen.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>When is Charlotte Restaurant Week?</summary>
        <p>Queen&#8217;s Feast runs twice a year — ten days each January and July — with three-course prix fixe menus at more than 120 restaurants across the region. <a href="/explore-charlotte-restaurant-week-july-2026-dining-guide/">Our Restaurant Week guide</a> covers how to pick your reservations.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

